# ZCU208 Linux Play/Capture Verification Procedure (PetaLinux 2025.2 port, offline site)

Conventions:
- `PC$` is a command on the site Linux PC.
- `ZCU#` is a command on the board as root.
- No internet is needed: every tool used here is either in the PetaLinux rootfs or standard on a Linux PC.

## 1. Items to carry

| Item | Location |
|---|---|
| SD image | `carry_26_09_final/wic/petalinux-sdimage.wic` |
| Boot fallback | `carry_26_09_final/BOOT/` (`BOOT.BIN`, `boot.scr`, `image.ub`) |
| Rootfs fallback | `carry_26_09_final/rootfs/rootfs.tar.gz` |
| Vitis apps | `carry_26_09_final/apps/` (`wave.elf`, `rfdcapi.elf`) |
| Checksums | `carry_26_09_final/MD5SUMS` |
| Analysis script | `analyze_cap.py` (section 13), saved to the USB stick beforehand |

**Hardware:** ZCU208 + CLK104 + XM655, SD card (8 GB or larger) and reader, micro-USB (UART), Ethernet cable, SMA cables, attenuator/DC block, oscilloscope or spectrum analyzer.

## 2. Address reference

| Address | Block | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `0xA0000000` | RFDC registers | `librfdc` |
| `0xA0040000` | `axi_gpio_spi_mux` | rfclks GPIO ID source |
| `0xA0060000` | `adc_gpio_0` | Capture trigger |
| `0xA0070000` | `dac_gpio` | Playback enable |
| `0xA0080000` | `hier_play` BRAM (128 KB) | `file2player` |
| `0xA00A0000` | `hier_cap0` BRAM (128 KB) | `cap2file` ch0 |
| `0xA00C0000` | `hier_cap1` BRAM (128 KB) | `cap2file` ch1 |

**Signal path:** DAC tile 228 `vout00`/`vout10`; ADC tile 226 `vin20`/`vin30`.

## 3. Verify the carried files (PC)

```bash
PC$ cd /path/to/carry_26_09_final
PC$ md5sum -c MD5SUMS                  # all lines must say OK
```

## 4. Write the SD card (PC)

```bash
PC$ lsblk                              # identify the SD card, e.g. /dev/sdX (check size!)
PC$ sudo umount /dev/sdX?* 2>/dev/null
PC$ sudo dd if=wic/petalinux-sdimage.wic of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress conv=fsync
PC$ sync
PC$ lsblk /dev/sdX                     # expect 2 partitions (FAT boot + ext4 root)
PC$ sudo eject /dev/sdX
```

**Fallback, only if the WIC doesn't boot:**

```bash
PC$ sudo parted /dev/sdX --script mklabel msdos mkpart primary fat32 4MiB 1GiB mkpart primary ext4 1GiB 100%
PC$ sudo mkfs.vfat -F 32 -n BOOT /dev/sdX1
PC$ sudo mkfs.ext4 -F -L root /dev/sdX2
PC$ sudo mkdir -p /mnt/sdb /mnt/sdr
PC$ sudo mount /dev/sdX1 /mnt/sdb && sudo cp BOOT/* /mnt/sdb/
PC$ sudo mount /dev/sdX2 /mnt/sdr && sudo tar -xzpf rootfs/rootfs.tar.gz -C /mnt/sdr
PC$ sync && sudo umount /mnt/sdb /mnt/sdr
```

## 5. Hardware setup

1. Board power off. Set the boot mode switch to **SD** (see UG1410 for the switch position).
2. Fit the CLK104 and XM655. Connect micro-USB (UART), Ethernet (PC ↔ board directly), and power.
3. **Play test:** XM655 `vout00` SMA → instrument.
4. **Capture test:** XM655 `vout00` → attenuator/DC block → `vin20` SMA.

## 6. Serial console (PC)

```bash
PC$ ls /dev/ttyUSB*                    # ZCU208 FTDI exposes 4 ports
PC$ sudo screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200    # if nothing at boot, try ttyUSB1..3
#   (exit screen: Ctrl-A then K, then y)
#   alternatives: sudo picocom -b 115200 /dev/ttyUSB1   |   sudo minicom -D /dev/ttyUSB1 -b 115200
```

Power on the board and watch U-Boot, then the kernel, then the login prompt.

## 7. Login and root shell (board, via serial)

PetaLinux 2025.2 normally uses user `petalinux` and asks you to set a password on first login.

```bash
ZCU# sudo -i                           # all following ZCU# commands as root
ZCU# uname -a
ZCU# cat /proc/cmdline
```

## 8. Network, no DHCP (PC + board)

```bash
PC$  ip link                                         # find PC interface name, e.g. enp3s0
PC$  sudo ip addr flush dev enp3s0
PC$  sudo ip addr add 192.168.1.1/24 dev enp3s0
PC$  sudo ip link set enp3s0 up

ZCU# ip addr flush dev eth0
ZCU# ip addr add 192.168.1.10/24 dev eth0
ZCU# ip link set eth0 up
ZCU# ping -c 3 192.168.1.1
PC$  ping -c 3 192.168.1.10
```

## 9. Deploy the Vitis apps (PC → board)

If root SSH login is disabled, copy to the `petalinux` home directory first:

```bash
PC$  scp apps/wave.elf apps/rfdcapi.elf petalinux@192.168.1.10:/home/petalinux/
ZCU# cp /home/petalinux/wave.elf /home/petalinux/rfdcapi.elf /usr/bin/
ZCU# chmod +x /usr/bin/wave.elf /usr/bin/rfdcapi.elf
```

If SSH key or host-key prompts get in the way, add `-o StrictHostKeyChecking=no` to `scp`.

Sanity check on the board:

```bash
ZCU# ls -l /usr/lib/librfdc.so.13* /usr/lib/libmetal.so.1*
ZCU# which rfclks file2player cap2file wave.elf rfdcapi.elf
ZCU# ldd /usr/bin/rfdcapi.elf          # every line must resolve, none "not found"
ZCU# mkdir -p /root/run && cd /root/run
```

## 10. Topology capture (board; always do this)

```bash
ZCU# { date; uname -a
       echo "--- gpio";   ls /sys/class/gpio/
       echo "--- gpiochip labels"; for c in /sys/class/gpio/gpiochip*; do echo "$c base=$(cat $c/base) ngpio=$(cat $c/ngpio) label=$(cat $c/label)"; done
       echo "--- i2c";    ls -l /dev/i2c-*; i2cdetect -l
       echo "--- platform"; ls /sys/bus/platform/devices/ | grep -iE "a00|rf"
     } 2>&1 | tee /root/run/topology.log

ZCU# grep a0040000 /root/run/topology.log      # → base=N  ← this N is the rfclks GPIO ID
```

**Checks:**
- `/sys/class/gpio` exists.
- A gpiochip with label `a0040000.gpio` exists.
- `/dev/i2c-20` exists.

## 11. Program the clocks (board)

```bash
ZCU# rfclks <N> 2>&1 | tee /root/run/rfclks.log
ZCU# grep -iE "error|fail" /root/run/rfclks.log   # expect nothing
```

**Pass:** `rfclks: using GPIO ID <N>` with no `i2c init` / `gpio init` / `spi init` errors.

**If it fails:**

```bash
ZCU# dmesg | tail -40 | tee /root/run/dmesg_rfclks.log
```

Stop here and bring the logs back.

## 12. RFDC bring-up (board)

```bash
ZCU# rfdcapi.elf 2>&1 | tee /root/run/rfdcapi.log
```

If it's menu-driven, choose the tile status and startup options. Pass criterion: DAC tile 228 and ADC tile 226 have their PLLs locked and are in state 15 (running).

Quick register-level check, to show the RFDC IP is alive:

```bash
ZCU# devmem 0xA0000000 32              # IP version register, non-zero
```

## 13. DAC playback (board + instrument)

Generate the waveform:

```bash
ZCU# wave.elf                          # no args → prints usage; note required parameters
ZCU# wave.elf <args per usage> 2>&1 | tee /root/run/wave.log
ZCU# ls -l /root/run                   # note generated file name + size
```

Load and enable:

```bash
ZCU# file2player                       # no args → prints usage
ZCU# file2player <wave_file> 0xA0080000 <args per usage> 2>&1 | tee /root/run/play.log
ZCU# devmem 0xA0070000 32 1            # play enable
ZCU# devmem 0xA0070000 32              # read back → 0x00000001
```

**Check on the instrument:**
- Tone at the expected frequency.
- Sane amplitude.
- No glitch at the BRAM wrap point.
- Take a screenshot.

Disable and check that the output stops:

```bash
ZCU# devmem 0xA0070000 32 0
```

Re-enable playback for the capture test:

```bash
ZCU# devmem 0xA0070000 32 1
```

## 14. ADC capture with loopback (board)

```bash
ZCU# devmem 0xA0060000 32 0            # trigger low
ZCU# devmem 0xA0060000 32 1            # rising edge → capture
ZCU# cap2file                          # no args → usage check
ZCU# cap2file /root/run/cap0.bin 0xA00A0000 128 2>&1 | tee /root/run/cap.log
ZCU# cap2file /root/run/cap1.bin 0xA00C0000 128 2>&1 | tee -a /root/run/cap.log
ZCU# ls -l /root/run/cap*.bin          # expect 131072 bytes each
ZCU# hexdump -C /root/run/cap0.bin | head -20   # non-zero, varying values
```

Package everything and copy it to the PC:

```bash
ZCU# cd /root && tar -czf run_$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M).tar.gz run/
PC$  scp petalinux@192.168.1.10:/root/run_*.tar.gz .    # or copy via /home/petalinux first
PC$  tar -xzf run_*.tar.gz
```

## 15. Analysis on the PC (offline)

Save this as `analyze_cap.py` before you go. It needs Python 3 with numpy (and optionally matplotlib).

```python
import sys, numpy as np
fn = sys.argv[1]; fs = float(sys.argv[2]) if len(sys.argv) > 2 else 1.0   # fs in Hz (1.0 = normalized)
x = np.fromfile(fn, dtype='<i2').astype(float)
print(f"samples={len(x)} min={x.min():.0f} max={x.max():.0f} mean={x.mean():.1f} rms={x.std():.1f}")
w = np.hanning(len(x)); X = np.abs(np.fft.rfft((x - x.mean()) * w))
k = np.argmax(X[1:]) + 1
print(f"peak bin={k}  f={k*fs/len(x):.6g} Hz  ({20*np.log10(X[k]/X.sum()):.1f} dB rel)")
try:
    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
    f = np.arange(len(X)) * fs / len(x)
    plt.subplot(211); plt.plot(x[:1000]); plt.title(fn)
    plt.subplot(212); plt.plot(f, 20*np.log10(X + 1e-9)); plt.xlabel('Hz'); plt.show()
except ImportError:
    pass
```

```bash
PC$ python3 -c "import numpy; print(numpy.__version__)"   # confirm numpy exists offline
PC$ python3 analyze_cap.py run/cap0.bin <ADC_Fs_Hz>
PC$ python3 analyze_cap.py run/cap1.bin <ADC_Fs_Hz>
```

**Without numpy**, check that the data looks sane:

```bash
PC$ od -An -t d2 -v run/cap0.bin | head -20
```

## 16. Pass/fail summary

| Step | Pass criterion | Result |
|---|---|---|
| SD/boot | Login prompt | |
| Network | Ping both ways | |
| Apps | `ldd` shows no "not found" | |
| Topology | `/sys/class/gpio`, `a0040000` gpiochip, `/dev/i2c-20` | |
| rfclks | No init errors | |
| rfdcapi | Tiles 226/228 locked, state 15 | |
| Play | Expected tone on instrument, stops on disable | |
| Capture | `cap0.bin` peak at the expected frequency | |

## 17. Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Command | Likely cause |
|---|---|---|
| No console output | Try `ttyUSB0`–`ttyUSB3` | Wrong port, or boot switch not on SD |
| No ping | `ip addr`, `ip link` on both sides | Interface name, or link down |
| `scp` refused as root | Use `petalinux@`, then `cp` as root | Root SSH disabled |
| `rfclks` i2c init fails | `i2cdetect -l` | Bridge isn't `i2c-20` |
| `rfclks` gpio init fails | `ls /sys/class/gpio`; check base N | Wrong N, or no sysfs |
| `rfclks` spi init fails | `dmesg \| tail` | Mux/bridge path. Save the logs |
| Tiles don't lock | Re-run `rfclks`, then `rfdcapi` | Clocks not programmed |
| Shared library error | `ldd /usr/bin/rfdcapi.elf` | Missing `.so` in the rootfs |
| `mmap` / `/dev/mem` error | `id`; `dmesg \| tail` | Not root |
| No DAC output | `devmem 0xA0070000 32` | Play not enabled, wrong SMA, or tiles not running |
| Capture all zeros | Re-send the 0→1 trigger; check play | No trigger, or no input |

